  "summary_en": "Grunge Pine Bark generates a pattern of layered noise resembling pine tree bark. It serves as a building block for more intricate textures, such as flaky bark for trees or wooden furniture.",
  "inputs": [
    "size_ref: representative layer that sets the output size and metadata"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Range: Amplitude multiplies values (originally 0 to 1), Center offsets them, Mask Contrast increases extremes first",
    "Pattern: Element Size, Element Scale (with Per-Component Controls), Offset, Tile Size",
    "Bark Intensity: how much of the bark is covered by the secondary vertical scale cells",
    "Bark Size: scale of those cells; higher values give fewer, larger scales",
    "Bark Roughness: bumpy, alligator-like detail of the base layer",
    "Post Processing, applied in order: Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Output can fall below 0 or above 1; use Clamp Minimum and Clamp Maximum",
    "Complement works as expected only for values from 0 to 1",
    "Fold has no effect when all values are positive",
    "Post-processing Contrast is not the same as Noise Contrast"
  ],
  "resume_fr": "Grunge Pine Bark produit un motif d'écorce de pin par bruits superposés, utile pour une écorce écaillée ou un meuble en bois."
